From 7ea9e65b2da7ee1723bef0f2a0bd9cbb56907b4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cerXXXX <polyakovia2009@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:23:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: scene clocks, compose layers and property scripts

Fixes found on workshop scene 3299228616 (clock + audio bars), all generic:

- compose layers honor "copybackground": false (CLEARALPHA on the copy pass),
  otherwise effects like scroll/fisheye show a shifted copy of the background
  (the "broken squares" over the clock)
- objects honor their parents' visibility, wallpapers hide whole groups
  (per language, per clock position) through the parent
- text objects: parent transforms, Y axis/rotation like images, size in
  points at 300 DPI rasterized at the on-scene size, UTF-8, monospace system
  font for systemfont_consolas/courier, opacity from alpha
- integer colors that are all <= 1 ("1 1 1" in project.json) are normalized
  colors, not 0-255
- property scripts actually run: keep the module namespace (JS_Eval of a
  module never exposed update ()), register the module before its top level
  runs so createScriptProperties () works, every script gets its own
  thisLayer, thisLayer properties can be read and assigned, returned bools
  and vectors convert properly and undefined keeps the value
- thisLayer.getTextureAnimation () with setFrame/getFrame/frameCount/play/
  pause/stop/isPlaying, pinned frames are used by the sprite sheet pass
- the first exception of every script is logged once

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
